  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "R.Suresh Kumar vs The District Collector on 14 February, 2024 Author: D. Krishnakumar Bench: D. Krishnakumar, R.Vijayakumar W.P(MD)No.15 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 14.02.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice D. Krishnakumar and The Honourable Mr.Justice R.Vijayakumar W.P(MD)No.1526 of 2024 R.Suresh Kumar ... Petitioner vs. 1.The District Collector, Madurai District, Madurai. 2.The Superintendent of Police, Madurai District, Madurai. 3.The Deputy Superintendent of Police, Prohibition Enforcement Wing, Madurai Zone, Madurai. 4.The Deputy Superintendent of Police, Melur, Madurai. 5.The Block Development Officer, Melur Union, Melur, Madurai District. 6.The Director, Food Safety Department, Viswanathapuram, Madurai. 1/6 R.Suresh Kumar vs The District Collector on 14 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/68311314/ 1 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W. 7.The Inspector of Police, Melur Police Station, Madurai District. ... Respon PRAYER : Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of I praying for issuance of a Writ of Mandamus, directing the respondents t initiate action against the illegal selling of liquor and gutka in the the scheme for women through self help groups situated at fifth respondent's office campus . For Petitioner : Mr.R.Aravindan For Respondent Nos.1 & 6 : Mr.P.Thilak Kumar Government Pleader For Respondent No.2 to 4 & 7 : Mr.R.Meenakshi Sunda Additional Public Pr ORDER (Order of the Court was made by D. KRISHNAKUMAR, J.)",
    "facts": "The petitioner has filed the present Writ Petition for issuance of a Writ of Mandamus, to direct the respondents to initiate action against the illegal selling of liquor and gutka in the shop under the scheme for women through self help groups situated at fifth respondent's office campus. 2.When the matter came up for hearing on 24.01.2024, this Court passed the following order: 'It is the case of the petitioner that one P.C.Pandi, who is running a tea shop at the campus of Block Development Office, Melur under the Scheme for Women through Self Help Groups, indulged in unlawful activity by selling liquor and gutka to the general public and several criminal cases have been registered as against him under Section 4(1a) of Prohibition Act and subsequently, the said shop was locked and sealed by the Officer of Food Safety Department on 30.11.2023. In this regard, the petitioner has also sent representation to initiate action against the illegal selling of liquor and Gutka in Tea shop. Hence, the petitioner has filed this Writ Petition.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
